From 41221bb685340d25e7c718502e9684baa01024a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dalton Singleton <blumoon94@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:12:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Cache the window's display index; write diagnostics on a
 background thread

Stardew asks for the window's display index every frame. On Haiku each
SDL call is an app_server round trip (about 1 ms, ~5% of frame time), so
cache it for half a second.

The frame and content-load profilers opened, wrote and closed their CSV
files for every sample, which cost tens of milliseconds per frame on
Haiku and distorted the frame times they measured. Queue the lines and
write them from a background thread with the files kept open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AVRp8nockFeWgKbb4pQJh9
